  "review": {
    "book": "NUM",
    "entityID": "person:korah_1795",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now Korah, the son of Izhar, the son of Kohath, the son of Levi, with Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab, and On, the son of Peleth, sons of Reuben, took some men."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "He said to Korah and to all his company, “In the morning, the LORD will show who are his, and who is holy, and will cause him to come near to him. Even him whom he shall choose, he will cause to come near to him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "Do this: have Korah and all his company take censers,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Moses said to Korah, “Hear now, you sons of Levi!"
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "Moses said to Korah, “You and all your company go before the LORD, you, and they, and Aaron, tomorrow."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "Korah assembled all the congregation opposite them to the door of the Tent of Meeting. The LORD’s glory appeared to all the congregation."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Speak to the congregation, saying, ‘Get away from around the tent of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram!’”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:27",
        "textualBasisJa": "So they went away from the tent of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram, on every side. Dathan and Abiram came out, and stood at the door of their tents with their wives, their sons, and their little ones."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:32",
        "textualBasisJa": "The earth opened its mouth and swallowed them up with their households, all of Korah’s men, and all their goods."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:40",
        "textualBasisJa": "to be a memorial to the children of Israel, to the end that no stranger who isn’t of the offspring of Aaron, would come near to burn incense before the LORD, that he not be as Korah and as his company; as the LORD spoke to him by Moses."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:49",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now those who died by the plague were fourteen thousand seven hundred, in addition to those who died about the matter of Korah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 26:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "The sons of Eliab: Nemuel, Dathan, and Abiram. These are that Dathan and Abiram who were called by the congregation, who rebelled against Moses and against Aaron in the company of Korah when they rebelled against the LORD;"
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 26:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "and the earth opened its mouth, and swallowed them up together with Korah when that company died; at the time the fire devoured two hundred fifty men, and they became a sign."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 26:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "Notwithstanding, the sons of Korah didn’t die."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 27:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Our father died in the wilderness. He was not among the company of those who gathered themselves together against the LORD in the company of Korah, but he died in his own sin. He had no sons."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 16:31",
        "textualBasisJa": "As he finished speaking all these words, the ground that was under them split apart."
      }
    ],
